WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.534
Guys, it can be hard
to say goodbye,

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.937
but sometimes you have to,
and there are a few things

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.905
I'd like to say goodbye to
right now.

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.540
It's time for "Go On, Git."

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.242
-♪ Go on, git ♪

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:12.178
♪ Go on, git ♪

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:17.250
♪ Go on, go on, go on, git ♪

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.819
[ Western electric guitar
twanging ]

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:23.256
♪♪

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:26.325
-Go on, git, Super Bowl ads

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:28.227
that keep airin'
after the Super Bowl.

00:00:28.227 --> 00:00:29.962
You're like the weird
20-year-old

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:32.065
who still hangs out
at his old high school.

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:34.433
It's over, hoss!

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:36.368
Seein' you try
to relive your glory

00:00:36.368 --> 00:00:40.206
during a rerun of "NCIS"
just makes me S-A-D.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:43.509
Now learn something from
those Budweiser frogs and...

00:00:43.509 --> 00:00:45.478
[Croaking] Go. On. Git.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.380
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.848
[ Applause ]

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.551
♪♪

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.486
Go on, git!

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.254
Keys.

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:56.722
It's 2021.

00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:58.191
Why am I still walking around

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:01.761
with a bunch of tiny
jagged knifes in my pocket?

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:04.363
Make me sound like sleigh bells.

00:01:04.363 --> 00:01:06.966
Even Motel 6 upgraded
to the key card,

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.369
and they can't even afford
water pressure!

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:11.403
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.403 --> 00:01:14.140
So, keys, uh, go on...

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.776
use yourselves
to unlock the door, then git.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.978
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:26.118
♪♪

00:01:26.118 --> 00:01:33.259
♪♪

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.894
Go on, git.

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.563
Seeds.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:38.197
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:39.932
I see you tryin'
to act like a food,

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:43.168
sneakin' your way into salads
and smoothies and whatnot.

00:01:43.168 --> 00:01:44.870
But y'all ain't food!

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:47.006
You go into the ground
and become food!

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:48.641
You are pre-food!

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.810
So go on, git,
back into the ground, seeds,

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:54.413
and come back when you're an
actual full-grown sunflower.

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:56.582
And then I'll eatcha!

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.083
And then I'll eatcha!

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.619
And then I'll eatcha!

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:03.222
And then I'll eatcha!

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.024
Then I'll eatcha!

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:08.060
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:12.565
[ Spitting, can dinging ]

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:15.001
Sunflower, I'll eat you!

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.902
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.902 --> 00:02:19.305
[ Laughs ]

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.973
Go on, git...

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:22.441
[ Laughs ]

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:25.378
...TV shows where sound effects

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:27.713
are way louder
than the talkin' parts.

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:30.416
When I'm immersin' myself
into a make-believe world

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.385
of double-crossing CIA agents,

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:33.886
I want to relax, not play a game

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:36.355
of volume chess
with my TV remote.

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:40.793
So GO ON, git, BACK to
ONE CONSISTENT VOLUME!

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:43.195
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:43.195 --> 00:02:47.900
♪♪

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.969
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:54.073
♪♪

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:57.910
Go on, git, thesauruses.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.679
You are unnecessary,
superfluous,

00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:02.482
heck, even redundant.

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:05.551
But, hey, since you like
pretty words so much,

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.053
I got a couple for ya.

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:09.155
Abdicate your position.

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:11.090
[ Applause ]

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:17.029
♪♪

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:22.935
♪♪

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:26.405
Go on, git! Crab cakes.

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:29.575
When I hear the word "cake," I
think of a sweet, spongy treat.

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:31.110
But when I hear the word "crab,"

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:35.080
I think of the ocean's
scariest STD.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.583
And that's a no-go
for my appetito.

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:40.018
So go on, git, crab cakes,
and come back when you're

00:03:40.018 --> 00:03:43.022
tiny cakes for crabs
'cause that'd be adorable.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.624
Well, it's hard to see 'em go,

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.592
but I'm glad I got that
out of my system.

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:49.128
We'll be right back with
Dwayne Johnson, everybody.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.930
[ Spits, can dings ]

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:58.605 line:0%
♪♪

